IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vmu-nouns`

-- Section 10: Notification of fees and penalties.
-- The duty is the Minister's: "must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts" and says that the notice is to be given so that the amounts "are notified to the public generally or to the sector of the public likely to be affected".
-- For the person who sets or applies a fee or a penalty it says whether the notice is owed.
-- "reasonable steps" is a judgment the text leaves open, so it is asked as a fact.
-- The duty is limited in its own words to the Minister responsible for administering the instrument; for anyone else the text says neither yes nor no, so NOTHING.

§ `Section 10 -- Notification of fees and penalties`

-- src:113 | (1) The Minister responsible for administering an Act or a statutory rule that provides for fees or penalties by fee units or penalty units must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of those fees and penalties calculated in accordance with section 7 are notified to the public generally or to the sector of the public likely to be affected by the fee or penalty.
@ref s 10(1) (src:113)
GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
      `the instrument provides for fees or penalties by fee units or penalty units` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Minister responsible for administering the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(1) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts is given` MEANS
    IF     `the instrument is an Act or a statutory rule`
       AND `the instrument provides for fees or penalties by fee units or penalty units`
       AND `the person is the Minister responsible for administering the instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the instrument is an Act or a statutory rule` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the instrument`
            WHEN `an Act` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a statutory rule` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a legislative instrument` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `an instrument of another kind` THEN FALSE

-- Where the duty arises, the Minister has met it if reasonable steps were taken to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts, calculated in accordance with section 7,
-- was notified to the public generally or to the sector of the public likely to be affected.
-- src:113 | (1) The Minister responsible for administering an Act or a statutory rule that provides for fees or penalties by fee units or penalty units must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of those fees and penalties calculated in accordance with section 7 are notified to the public generally or to the sector of the public likely to be affected by the fee or penalty.
@ref s 10(1) (src:113)
GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
      `the instrument provides for fees or penalties by fee units or penalty units` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Minister responsible for administering the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable steps were taken to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts calculated in accordance with section 7 was notified to the public generally or to the sector likely to be affected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(1) -- the Minister has taken the steps that the subsection requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 10(1) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts is given` `the instrument` `the instrument provides for fees or penalties by fee units or penalty units` `the person is the Minister responsible for administering the instrument`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST duty THEN JUST (duty AND `reasonable steps were taken to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts calculated in accordance with section 7 was notified to the public generally or to the sector likely to be affected`)

-- "an Act or a statutory rule under which a legislative instrument is made that provides for fees by fee units": fees only, and the duty is the same.
-- src:115 | (2) The Minister responsible for administering an Act or a statutory rule under which a legislative instrument is made that provides for fees by fee units must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of those fees calculated in accordance with section 7 are notified to the public generally or to the sector of the public likely to be affected by the fee.
@ref s 10(2) (src:115)
GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
      `a legislative instrument made under the instrument provides for fees by fee units` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Minister responsible for administering the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(2) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of the fees is given` MEANS
    IF     `the instrument is an Act or a statutory rule`
       AND `a legislative instrument made under the instrument provides for fees by fee units`
       AND `the person is the Minister responsible for administering the instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the instrument is an Act or a statutory rule` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the instrument`
            WHEN `an Act` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a statutory rule` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a legislative instrument` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `an instrument of another kind` THEN FALSE

-- src:115 | (2) The Minister responsible for administering an Act or a statutory rule under which a legislative instrument is made that provides for fees by fee units must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of those fees calculated in accordance with section 7 are notified to the public generally or to the sector of the public likely to be affected by the fee.
@ref s 10(2) (src:115)
GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
      `a legislative instrument made under the instrument provides for fees by fee units` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Minister responsible for administering the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable steps were taken to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of the fees calculated in accordance with section 7 was notified to the public generally or to the sector likely to be affected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(2) -- the Minister has taken the steps that the subsection requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 10(2) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of the fees is given` `the instrument` `a legislative instrument made under the instrument provides for fees by fee units` `the person is the Minister responsible for administering the instrument`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST duty THEN JUST (duty AND `reasonable steps were taken to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of the fees calculated in accordance with section 7 was notified to the public generally or to the sector likely to be affected`)
